- op: discuss  # 7eea
  at: '2026-08-27T23:11:31Z'  # 7eea
  by: agent  # 7eea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7eea
  clock: 4  # 7eea
  nonce: 7eea  # 7eea
  message: "DERIVED: 24.1% useful (27 of 112), not the published <=25.0%. Committed as 607a99ea2e\n(0006 gains a \"Useful precision, re-derived\" section; the index row and ADR-0046 are\ncorrected). Derivation is machine-checkable: gibom_08272026/derive.py reads 0006's own\nledger-final.json + pass4-summary.json, asserts the population matches the headline 38,\nand computes every figure. No count is hand-copied.\n\nTHE ITEM'S PREMISE HELD. <=25.0% first appears in bd638f8cbf -- the commit that published\n0008, a day after 0006 -- and 0006's own body supports 29.5% (5 named removals of 38/112).\nThe bound survives as a bound (24.1% <= 25.0%), so no prior decision needs revisiting; what\nwas missing was the working, not the answer.\n\nCLASS SPLIT, reported separately per ADR-0046:\n  KIND-MISDECLARED  11   CONFIGURED-ACTION  0\n  5 = shellcheck's haskell IORef/STRef under db_read (the 5 the record named)\n  6 = bash \"> /dev/null\"-only findings: cert-manager#0/#1/#2/#3, spacedrive#6,\n      guacamole-client#3. Each cited to the line. Live at measurement time; fixed\n      the next day by PR #541.\n\nCONFIGURED-ACTION IS ZERO, AND THAT REFUTES WHAT THIS ITEM AND ADR-0046 BOTH PREDICTED.\nBoth said \"expect it worse because the CONFIGURED-ACTION deduction was never applied.\"\nIt does not apply to this population at all, structurally: 0006's claim set admits only\nenv_read and host_info_read sources, so ADR-0046 clause 2 (deserialization into a type\nwhose fields are DECLARED as a configuration schema) has no candidate to match. The class\nis real but concentrated in config-file-driven servers like caddy -- 0005's cohort, not\n0006's. The number did fall 33.9% -> 24.1%; every point is KIND-MISDECLARED.\nNEAREST MISS disclosed: cilium#6 reads os.Getenv(SockPathEnv) and dials the socket it\nnames. Clauses 1 and 3 cite; clause 2 does not, so it counts USEFUL.\n\nA REVERSAL, recorded because only the second check caught it. gocryptfs#2 was first\nlabelled discard-only on four /dev/null sites. A raw re-read of test.bash found a fifth:\nL42 exec 200> \"$LOCKFILE\", a numbered-fd redirect to a real path, env-derived via\nTMPDIR -> TESTDIR -> LOCKFILE. Genuine env-to-filesystem write. The first cut would have\npublished 23.2%.\n\nDECLARED RATHER THAN DEDUCTED -- three unruled vocabulary questions, because INV-nular\nsays in terms that python parse_args/sys.argv and elixir Application.get_env under\nenv_read are \"DOCUMENTED deliberate choices in their rows, not oversights\" that \"need a\nvocabulary ruling, not a row edit\". Deducting them would be this record inventing the\nruling. Sized, with arithmetic:\n  S1 argv under env_read                10 members -> 15.2%\n  S2 application config under env_read   5 members -> 19.6%\n  S3 io_lib:format as a logging sink     3 members -> 21.4%  (subset of S2)\n  all resolved against                  15 members -> 10.7%\nSo the band is tripped at 24.1% and would be tripped far harder if the ruling goes against\nthe current rows. No reading of the evidence puts useful precision above 25%.\n\nLIMITATION STATED IN THE RECORD: one adjudicator, not a panel. 0006's 33.9% carries two\nindependent 16-agent panels plus adjudication plus adversarial refutation; this vacuity\nlabelling has none of that. Its protection is that every verdict is a citation a reader\ncan check.\n\nINV-duvup is unblocked on this gate."  # 7eea
